{"parentUuid":"6e7128e0-d5a1-4e08-97f3-39293c8c77ef","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChHYYVHCbmHSPDzb1HKCq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"They go in a `.env` file on the Vultr server, at **`/opt/hackwestern/.env`**. Vultr itself has no env-var settings panel. Docker Compose loads that file (`env_file: .env` in [docker-compose.yml:22](docker-compose.yml#L22)), and [docker-compose.prod.yml:4](docker-compose.prod.yml#L4) says `SITE_ADDRESS`, the API keys and `LIVE_JOBS_TOKEN` are read from it.\n\n```bash\nssh root@155.138.154.176          # or whatever DEPLOY_HOST is in the Makefile\ncd /opt/hackwestern\nnano .env                         # paste KEY=value lines, one per line\nchmod 600 .env\n```\n\nThen run `make deploy` from your machine, or run the compose `up -d --build web backend cad` command on the server. The containers only read the new values when they're recreated.\n\nKeep `.env` out of git. `make deploy` runs `git pull`, and a tracked `.env` would either overwrite the server's copy or put your keys in the repo."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":584,"cache_read_input_tokens":55352,"output_tokens":407,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":45},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":584,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":407,"cache_read_input_tokens":55352,"cache_creation_input_tokens":584,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":584},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"301cb2ab-b610-411f-8e87-d98542acd267","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChHYYV